<title>CSWeb Synchronization Service</title>


<subheader>Overview</subheader>

<link CSWeb::introduction_to_csweb.csdoc>CSWeb</link> is the preeminent CSPro synchronization option. It is a web server running the CSPro <link sync_services.csdoc>synchronization service</link> and is best suited for censuses and large surveys. CSWeb can be run on any web server with PHP and MySQL. It can be hosted on a headquarters computer, a hosted website, or a cloud-based virtual server. Configuring and maintaining a CSWeb server requires experience with web server <link CSWeb::best_practices.csdoc>administration</link> and cybersecurity. Users without these skills should consider using <link sync_service_dropbox.csdoc>Dropbox</link> or <link sync_service_ftp.csdoc>FTP</link> instead.


<seealso sync_services.csdoc />
